    "text": "Let G be a group of permutations of the set of positive integers N isomorphic\nto the additive group of rational numbers. Must there be an element g ∈ G such that\nthe set {a − ag | a ∈ N} is infinite?                                 N. M. Suchkov\n  ∗ Yes, it must (N. M. Suchkov, A. A. Shlepkin, D. A. Taysnyov, Siberian Math. J.,\n65 (2024), 1390–1394).",
